{
  "note": "Fixtures for /theme-lab (dev only). Each deck is hand-authored to be an unambiguous example of its archetype, with `expect` naming the theme slug(s) that SHOULD bubble to the top. Lands are mostly omitted: detection scores over non-land cards, so the manabase only dilutes the ratio uniformly. These are deliberately NOT EDHREC average decks — using our own data source as the test input would make the overlap signal circular. Twelve STRANGE decks were added deliberately — group hug, enchantress, stax/prison, ninjutsu, infect, toughness-matters, coin-flip chaos, squirrel tokens, curses, graveyard-permanents, storm and a tri-tribal Kaalia pile. Mainstream archetypes are the easy case; precision on the weird ones is the actual goal, and several of these deliberately probe known weak spots: rare mechanics that only ever appear on three or four cards (storm, infect), mutually-absorbing pairs (ninjas vs ninjutsu), and token tribes that exist almost entirely as tokens (squirrels).",
